# {{name}}

{{description}}

An AdminBolt panel plugin. It runs outside the panel, in its own process, and
ships on its own schedule.

## Develop

```bash
composer install
```

Create `runtime.json` next to `plugin.json`. The panel writes this at install
time; for development you write it yourself. It is gitignored.

```json
{
    "panel": { "url": "https://panel.example:2087" },
    "plugin": { "id": "{{id}}" },
    "api": { "key": "your-api-key", "secret": "your-api-secret" },
    "hooks": { "secret": "any-value-for-local-testing" },
    "settings": { "log_level": "debug" },
    "paths": { "data": "var/data", "logs": "var/logs" }
}
```

Run it, then send it a hook:

```bash
BOLT_PLUGIN_DIR="$PWD" php -S 127.0.0.1:8731 -t public public/index.php

bolt-plugin hook before_domain_creation --payload='{"domain":"example.invalid"}'
```

## Check and ship

```bash
composer test
bolt-plugin validate
bolt-plugin package
```

